WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.490
In 1858, a girl of 14,
Bernadette Soubirous,

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.920
reported visions at a
grotto in Lourdes, France.

3
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.720
A spring appeared there.

4
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:14.170
Today millions of pilgrims
visit, and some report healings.

5
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.990
In 2008, a French nun,
disabled for decades,

6
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.700
recovered suddenly after a pilgrimage.

7
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.700
So if a sick person recovers
and doctors can't explain it,

8
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.920
does that show God exists?

9
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:30.790
In this mission, you'll see how a
claimed cure at Lourdes is examined,

10
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.220
and read a healing from John's Gospel.

11
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:38.190
Then you'll face David Hume's famous
challenge to anyone who reports a miracle.

12
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.970
Your mission: weigh up whether a recovery
that doctors can't explain shows that

13
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.120
God exists.
